&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;11&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;20&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:3pt double #000;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Federal and State Income Tax Audit Status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;SWTCo and other AEP Subsidiaries are not currently under IRS audit and the statute of limitations (SOL) for the IRS to examine SWTCo and other AEP Subsidiaries originally filed federal return has expired for tax years prior to 2022. In July 2025, SWTCo and other AEP Subsidiaries received notification that its 2023 federal income tax return was selected for IRS examination. However, this examination has yet to begin.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Net Income Tax Operating Loss Carryforward&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;SWTCo had no federal net income tax operating loss carryforward ("NOLC") as of December 31, 2025 and 2024. As of December 31, 2025, SWTCo has state income tax net operating loss deferred tax assets as indicated in the table below. Management anticipates future taxable income will not be sufficient to realize the state net income tax operating loss tax benefits before the state carryforward expires, and has accrued a valuation allowance, fully offsetting the the future state tax benefit related to the NOLCs. These carryforwards will expire on various dates, see table below for detail:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:113.25pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:55.059%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:33.224%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.151%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:33.494%"/&gt;&lt;td